    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d6-a1-a1">

                <pb facs="0023" n="13" sameAs="frus:frus1864p1/pg13"/>

                <head>Mr. Adams to Earl Russell.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Legation of the United
                                States,</hi><hi rendition="#italic"> London,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1863-12-07"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 7, 1863.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord:</hi> With reference to your note of the 30th
                    November, respecting certain insinuations contained in the depositions of
                    parties at Queenstown against the conduct of Mr. Eastman, the consul of the
                    United States, in connexion with a supposed enlistment of men for service in the
                    steamer Kearsarge, I take pleasure in transmitting to you a copy of what Mr.
                    Eastman writes in answer to my inquiry.</p>
                <p>I pray your lordship to accept the assurances of the highest consideration with
                    which I have the honor to be, my lord, your most obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>CHARLES FRANCIS ADAMS.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>The Right Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Earl Russell</hi>,<hi
                            rendition="#italic"> &amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
